{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KnotComplement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KnotComplement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotComplement.h1Rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotComplement.h1Rank","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Rank of `H₁(S³ \\ K; ℤ) = ℤ` (always 1 for a knot). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotComplement.pi1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotComplement.pi1","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Wirtinger-style π₁ presentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotComplement.cuspShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotComplement.cuspShape","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Cusp shape modulus τ (positive imaginary part for hyperbolic\ncomplements). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotComplement.hyperbolicVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotComplement.hyperbolicVolume","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Hyperbolic volume `Vol(S³ \\ K)`.  Zero when the complement is\nnot hyperbolic (e.g. torus knots, unknot). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotComplement.name","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotComplement.name","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Display name of the knot (e.g. `\"4_1\"`, `\"trefoil\"`, `\"5_2\"`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotComplement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotComplement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotComplement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotComplement","kind":"structure","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L54-L74","doc":"**Knot complement** (visualiser data structure).\n\nLightweight Lean side of the SnapPea bridge: bundles the\ngeometric invariants the visualiser needs (hyperbolic volume,\ncusp shape, π₁ presentation, first homology rank) into a single\nserialisable record.  All fields are populated at runtime by\nthe SnapPea kernel; this Lean structure pins the schema. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:viz-knot-complement","label":"def:viz-knot-complement","md":"visualizer/overview/viz-knot-complement.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalGroupPresentation.relators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalGroupPresentation.relators","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Relators, each encoded as a list of `(generator-index, sign)`\npairs.  `sign = .pos` is the generator, `.neg` is its inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalGroupPresentation.numGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalGroupPresentation.numGenerators","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Number of generators in the presentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalGroupPresentation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalGroupPresentation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalGroupPresentation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalGroupPresentation","kind":"structure","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L43-L52","doc":"A presentation of the fundamental group of a knot complement\nin terms of `numGenerators` Wirtinger generators and a list of\nrelator words.  Generators are abstract; the SnapPea bridge\ninstantiates them concretely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CuspShape.im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CuspShape.im","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Imaginary part of the cusp modulus τ.  Strictly positive for\na genuinely-hyperbolic cusp. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CuspShape.re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CuspShape.re","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L38-L38","doc":"Real part of the cusp modulus τ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CuspShape.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CuspShape.mk","kind":"ctor","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CuspShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CuspShape","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotComplement.lean#L33-L41","doc":"Cusp shape of a hyperbolic knot complement: a complex modulus\n`τ = x + i y` (with `y > 0`) describing the conformal class of\nthe cusp torus.  SnapPea returns this as a pair of reals. ","signatureChunk":0}]}